plex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that $a=\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=2>0$ and ${e}^{at}={e}^{2t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, we have a spiral that is traversed toward infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ \n\nTherefore, since $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0,$ the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable spiral (source)}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427142 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166943 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f0b176c-c802-5b3b-85d0-dede602c9bf3" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Systems of Linear Differential Equations With Complex Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a177b1d-8f4d-5ce4-96d5-0641118ffbd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427001} {:answer/id #uuid "44d3d3bc-85e9-5891-a136-208e1a7ae81c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427009} {:answer/id #uuid "59791c19-fe10-5a49-8c0d-1483606ff223" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427016} {:answer/id #uuid "61bacac7-6dd5-50c2-956e-a48c2f0f54d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :ans